      "notes": "The verdict is well-constructed. Claim 1 (stated tier) is directly supported by the policy text. Claim 2 is labelled measurable but the quote contains 'projected' \u2014 this is a mild tier_integrity concern since Defra's forward budget figures are projections not confirmed outturn facts; however the claim itself acknowledges the projection language and the evidence_id source is a government/NFU report, so this is a warning rather than blocking. Claim 3 is correctly labelled projected and appropriately hedged. The core O12 reasoning \u2014 unfunded spending worsens near-term debt path absent evidence of offsetting fiscal returns \u2014 is sound and symmetric with how unfunded tax cuts would be treated. Advocacy sources (NFU, Wildlife Trusts) are correctly flagged and used only for context, not as the sole basis for the verdict. The magnitude (minor) is defensible at ~0.04% GDP. No motive attribution, no party identity leakage, no false balance issues. One warning: E7 is cited as 'measurable' but contains forward projections; consider reclassifying to 'projected' in a revision."
